# Banned-content patterns, one extended regex per line. '#' comments.
# Enforced by tools/check_banned.sh via .githooks/ (commits, pushes) and the
# PR workflow. This file is public: patterns describe CLASSES of secret and
# must never contain an actual secret -- a banned-strings file that contains
# the strings defeats itself the moment the repo is public.
#
# Personal identifiers
[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@(icloud|gmail|me|outlook|yahoo)\.com
/Users/[a-z_][a-z0-9_-]*
/home/[a-z_][a-z0-9_-]*
claude-[0-9]{3}
#
# Credential shapes
gh[opsu]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
sk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
xox[baprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}
-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY
Authorization: (Bearer|Basic) [A-Za-z0-9+/=_.-]{16,}
